      ],
      "solution": "$S_n = \\sum_{r=1}^{n-1} r(n-r) = n \\sum_{r=1}^{n-1} r - \\sum_{r=1}^{n-1} r^2$\n$= n \\frac{(n-1)n}{2} - \\frac{(n-1)n(2n-1)}{6} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{6} [3n - (2n-1)] = \\frac{n(n-1)(n+1)}{6} = \\frac{n^3 - n}{6}$.\nThus, $\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{6 S_n}{n^3} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{n^3 - n}{n^3} = 1$."
